        {
          "id": "source-axes-and-labels",
          "description": "Horizontal x and vertical y cross at the sole printed origin 0 and point in the positive directions. Printed x values: [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]; printed y values: -1, 1, 2, 3. There are no printed half-unit values, curve-name labels, point letters or units. Modern labels are offset to keep clear of strokes; for g, nonnegative x values move above their unchanged tick positions so the descending curve cannot obscure them. This side change is modern, not a source label-placement fact.",
