          "id": "source-solid-curve",
          "description": "One solid descending, flattening curve from the visible upper-left endpoint to the lower-right endpoint, with no interior reversal or separate plotted point markers; it passes through the drawn axis crossing. The bounded endpoints are retained at their observed grid intersections. Short connected source-pixel spans are a modern tracing regularization, not an exact function formula. The queried half-unit level is read against the source lattice before tracing; it is not drawn as a new guide or annotated answer. Raster thickness/skew leaves roughly 0.1 unit uncertainty between cells; no unprinted interior value is silently snapped to an integer or half-integer.",
